WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:00.700
Now that muddy

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.835
mess couldn't stop Diplo

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.870
from making it to his next concert.

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.072
The DJ posted to his Instagram

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:06.906
saying that he walked

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:07.440
six miles

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.708
through the mud out of the desert

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.477
before hitchhiking his way

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.378
out of the festival

00:00:11.378 --> 00:00:13.513
to make sure to make sure that he made it

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.647
to Washington, D.C.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:15.782
on time

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:24.057
And he was joined by Chris

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:25.558
Rock in the back of a truck

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:27.093
with a group of fans

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.162
Diplo made it to the airport, walking

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.296
barefoot on the tarmac

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.032
and posted to his Instagram, quote,

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.034
No one believed we would get to the days,

00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:36.102
would get to D.C. for the show tonight.

00:00:36.102 --> 00:00:37.170
But God did so.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.638
Joining us now is three time

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:40.640
Grammy Award winner Diplo.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.342
Welcome to the program.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.310
Hi. How are you guys doing?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:44.944
Good.

00:00:44.944 --> 00:00:46.246
So were you

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.081
barefoot and walking,

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:49.883
duct tape and bags walking?

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.051
What were we dealing with here in

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.452
terms of a plan to get out?

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:54.454
I try

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:55.121
to duck tape and

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:55.622
walking back

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.690
some pretty good boots that zippers

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.092
and sort of tires.

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:00.293
And they worked pretty well.

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:02.562
They they were caked with mud,

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:03.930
so they got pretty heavy.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.933
There were like £3 each at one point.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:08.802
So I had some pretty strong leg muscles

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:09.436
after that walk.

00:01:09.436 --> 00:01:11.838
But when you started to walk in the mud,

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:12.705
you kind of realize

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:14.074
you have to stay low to the ground.

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.341
And it's very slippery.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.010
And if you don't walk on

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.179
where it was chewed up from tire marks,

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.281
it's pretty easy to move out of there.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:23.016
What was it like watching you?

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:24.751
What was it like watching other people?

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:26.586
I mean, was there a lot of dialog

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.420
in between tents

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.721
for people actually debating,

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:29.956
should we leave? Should we stay

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:35.161
It was about Friday, I think at 11 p.m.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.629
I was having dinner

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.264
and our camp and our camp next door was

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.100
Chris Rock was there.

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:41.234
Cindy Crawford

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.002
Kaia Gerber, Austin Butler.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.070
Michael Key was a bunch of people

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.371
were there that were,

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.207
you know, living in that camp.

00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.475
And they had the news

00:01:48.475 --> 00:01:49.309
that there was no chance

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.276
of leaving tonight

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.212
because there's going to be

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:53.646
even more rain forecast.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.415
And the main issue

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:56.282
was getting a car out of

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.917
there is really impossible and it's money

00:01:57.917 --> 00:01:58.318
because you're going

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:58.985
get stuck in a plane

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.420
and a lot of cars stuck on the

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:01.754
on the on the playa.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:02.522
It's going to create

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.990
huge traffic jams

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.059
for the eventual exodus of people.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.161
So there was no information

00:02:08.161 --> 00:02:09.662
we had to check the 30 minute Twitter.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.930
And I think at 10 a.m.

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:11.931
we said let's regroup

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.133
and see if we can walk out of here.

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.501
And I was

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:15.034
I said, that's

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:15.935
the only way we can do

00:02:15.935 --> 00:02:17.770
it is we can walk out.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.706
And we planned an excursion

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:21.741
the next morning and I think we had out.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.610
Me and about 20 other people

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.944
and we just we just walked

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:26.312
and we didn't see many people on the road

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.148
and we just, we kept walking.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:29.883
They said the gate was closed.

00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:31.151
It's the general term for the gate.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.485
The gate was on the line cars.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.686
And because people come to Bernie

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:34.921
on the last day for the burn

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.789
to love the sun in the Saturday,

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.225
but there's no actual gate to

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:40.026
open or closed

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:42.295
it's just the matter of the mud ends

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:44.330
and a paved road begins

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.532
and that payroll goes to gridlock.

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:47.400
NAVARRO And we had to walk to about two

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.401
that paved road.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.802
Are you still in contact with

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:50.336
people there?

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:53.806
Most of my friends did get out.

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.108
I mean, a lot of the deejay friends

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.876
I had, Raul asked me how to do it,

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.011
and I give them all the bikes.

00:02:58.011 --> 00:02:59.712
And I think like ten of my friends

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.114
that were back to work this weekend

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:02.148
and this Labor Day weekend, of course,

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.349
we have to work.

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:04.384
We all made it out.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.185
A lot of my friends that are

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:06.386
some of them are still there in the camp.

00:03:06.386 --> 00:03:07.787
They're having a good time.

00:03:07.787 --> 00:03:09.422
They're waiting it out.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.890
You know, this this

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.158
the mud always dries up there.

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:13.092
It's the middle of the desert.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.160
You don't expect rain,

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.828
but if you have sunshine,

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:16.863
it can dry up in four

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.464
or 5 hours with direct stands.

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:20.300
And it has been overcast the whole time.

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.902
So it's been really hard to to dry out.

00:03:22.902 --> 00:03:24.404
The moment between deciding

00:03:24.404 --> 00:03:26.306
you were going to actually

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.473
launch the excursion

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:28.741
and the video that I think

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.642
everybody in the country

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.144
has seen up to this point.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:32.312
Including the what,

00:03:32.312 --> 00:03:33.680
seemingly random appearance of Chris

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:36.182
Rock as you strolled around the camera,

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:36.950
which wasn't so random

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:38.351
since he was in the camp next door.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:40.186
What what was that like, those hours?

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.020
What were you talking

00:03:41.020 --> 00:03:42.088
what were you guys doing

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:42.689
as you were kind

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:44.457
of making this trek towards

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:45.758
finally getting picked up?

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.060
I think so, yeah.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:48.361
I mean, for sure,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:49.629
Chris is going to have a huge bit

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:50.530
in his next

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.631
special about Burning Man

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.699
because he was really

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.868
bizarrely

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.036
scared of what what's going to happen.

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:57.604
He thought there was going

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:59.872
to be cannibalism and a day later and,

00:03:59.906 --> 00:04:00.506
you know, didn't know

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:01.140
think we're going to run out.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.642
Our camp is still our stuff.

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.077
But I said, look, man,

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:04.911
this is a great people

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:06.212
know what they're doing here.

00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:07.380
Everybody here is camping.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.116
They all have self-reliance

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:11.417
and we just said I was surprised

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.686
he had his New York Knicks check it out.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:14.821
And we just he just got up that

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.189
and started walking

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.557
and we walked about 3 hours

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:19.759
in the mud and he was happy.

00:04:19.759 --> 00:04:20.660
Was me,

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:21.995
I think Cindy Crawford walked with us,

00:04:21.995 --> 00:04:24.097
Kaia Gerber, Austin Butler,

00:04:25.265 --> 00:04:26.899
Randy Gerber,

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:27.900
a writer,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.968
a couple of producers

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:29.769
from TV, a couple people

00:04:29.769 --> 00:04:30.136
who just want

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:31.170
to get home to their children.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.473
And they didn't take no for an answer.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:34.140
We're just like, look,

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:34.774
we can make it out.

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.242
There's no one stopping us from walking.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:37.143
And, you know,

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:37.844
it was a challenge,

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:38.778
but it was honestly

00:04:38.778 --> 00:04:40.113
one of the highlights of the whole trip

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:40.847
